.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Peter Sweet and Eugene Parker (1957-1958) proposed the first quantitative model of magnetic reconnection: oppositely directed field lines are driven together into a long, thin resistive current sheet of length L, where finite conductivity \eta finally lets them break and reconnect. The relevant dimensionless control parameter is the Lundquist number S=Lv_A/\eta, the ratio of the resistive diffusion time L^2/\eta to the Alfven crossing time L/v_A. Mass conservation through the sheet&#x27;s narrow exit throttles the whole process to">

